  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "u07_l2_g1",
      "pattern": "A/V-아서/어서 (sabab)",
      "meaning_uz": "Sabab: '...-gani uchun', '...-b' (sababli)",
      "meaning_en": "Reason: 'because…', 'so…'",
      "explanation_md": "**-아서/어서** 6-2 darsda **ketma-ketlik** ma'nosida o'rgangan edik (건너**서** 가세요). Bu darsda u **sabab**ni bildiradi: o'zbekchadagi **\"...-gani uchun\"**, **\"...-ib\"**.\n\n**목이 아파서 왔어요.** — *Tomog'im og'rigani uchun keldim.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n- Oxirgi unli **ㅏ, ㅗ** → **-아서**: 많다 → **많아서**, 오다 → **와서**\n- Boshqa unlilar → **-어서**: 먹다 → **먹어서**, 늦다 → **늦어서**, 걸리다 → **걸려서**\n- **하다** → **해서**: 피곤하다 → **피곤해서**\n- **ㅡ 탈락**: 아프다 → **아파서**, 바쁘다 → **바빠서**\n- **ㅂ 불규칙**: 춥다 → **추워서**\n\n### Ikki muhim qoida\n\n1. **-아서/어서 oldidan o'tgan zamon qo'yilmaydi.** Zamon gap oxirida ko'rsatiladi:\n   - ~~늦었어서 택시를 탔어요~~ ❌ → **늦어서 택시를 탔어요** ✅\n2. **Gap oxiri buyruq (-(으)세요) yoki taklif bo'lmaydi:**\n   - ~~아파서 병원에 가세요~~ ❌\n   - **아파서 병원에 갔어요** ✅ (oddiy darak gap)\n\n### Uzr va minnatdorlik\n\nKundalik gapda juda ko'p uchraydi:\n\n- 늦**어서** 미안해요. — *Kechikkanim uchun kechirasiz.*\n- 도와줘**서** 고마워요. — *Yordam berganingiz uchun rahmat.*",
      "explanation_md_en": "We learned **-아서/어서** in lesson 6-2 with the meaning of **sequence** (건너**서** 가세요). In this lesson it gives **a reason**: English **\"because…\"** or **\"…, so…\"**.\n\n**목이 아파서 왔어요.** — *I came because my throat hurts.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n- Last vowel **ㅏ, ㅗ** → **-아서**: 많다 → **많아서**, 오다 → **와서**\n- Other vowels → **-어서**: 먹다 → **먹어서**, 늦다 → **늦어서**, 걸리다 → **걸려서**\n- **하다** → **해서**: 피곤하다 → **피곤해서**\n- **ㅡ drops**: 아프다 → **아파서**, 바쁘다 → **바빠서**\n- **ㅂ-irregular**: 춥다 → **추워서**\n\n### Two important rules\n\n1. **No past tense before -아서/어서.** The tense goes at the end of the sentence:\n   - ~~늦었어서 택시를 탔어요~~ ❌ → **늦어서 택시를 탔어요** ✅\n2. **The sentence can't end with a request (-(으)세요) or a suggestion:**\n   - ~~아파서 병원에 가세요~~ ❌\n   - **아파서 병원에 갔어요** ✅ (a plain statement)\n\n### Apologies and thanks\n\nVery common in everyday speech:\n\n- 늦**어서** 미안해요. — *Sorry I'm late.* (lit. because I'm late, I'm sorry)\n- 도와줘**서** 고마워요. — *Thank you for helping me.*",
      "formation": [
